  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Mary's Kitchen Notebook",
    "overview": "The Quesha display face gives the app a handwritten, homely warmth. Everything underneath it is plain and practical: table numbers, running orders, bills and cash counts, set in a sturdy sans on warm cream paper. The notebook is the kitchen's own. It is warm and a little personal, but it stays orderly, because the counter has to settle bills from it in a queue.\n\nDensity is moderate. Screens run from a phone-first waiter floor (table grid, bottom navigation, cart drawer) to a desktop counter and owner layout (collapsible roasted-brown sidebar with cards on cream). There is a full dark mode, toggled by a `.dark` class, which re-tones the palette to warm espresso rather than switching to neutral grey.\n\nThe system currently layers depth through soft shadows, gradient-filled primary buttons and hover lift. That is recorded below exactly as implemented and flagged as drift. It is more ornament than a billing tool needs.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Quesha, the handwritten display face, is used for headings and table numbers only. Everything operational is set in sans.",
      "Warm roasted-brown primaries on cream and off-white paper, with lily green for positive and settled states.",
      "Every tappable control is at least 48px. The floor is a touch surface.",
      "Money and counts are set in monospace or tabular numerals.",
      "Dark mode is espresso-warm, never cool grey.",
      "Motion is short, decelerating and informative: counts roll, finished things get one checkmark, nothing bounces."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Brown Means Go Rule",
        "body": "Roasted Coffee is the only colour for the primary action on a screen. Settled or paid outcomes get Lily Leaf, not brown.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Espresso Dark Rule",
        "body": "Dark mode re-tones every token to warm brown-black (page `#1C1812`, surface `#2A2419`, raised `#3A3128`, text `#F5F0E8`). Never introduce neutral greys (`neutral-800` and similar) in dark mode.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Readable Signal Rule",
        "body": "Status and Lily Leaf text always uses a token that passes 4.5:1 (`text-success`, `text-warning`, `text-error`, `text-info`, `text-lily-ink`). Never hard-code a hex to get a darker shade.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quesha Is a Heading Rule",
        "body": "Quesha is only for headings, brand wordmarks and table numbers. Never use it for prices, buttons, form labels or anything someone has to read under pressure.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Honest Numbers Rule",
        "body": "Rupee amounts, quantities and order numbers use `font-mono` or `tabular-nums`, so that columns of money line up.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The 48px Floor Rule",
        "body": "Every interactive control has a hit area of at least 48 × 48px (`--min-height-touch`, `touch-target-large`). This is non-negotiable on the waiter and count screens.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No New Shadows Rule",
        "body": "Don't add shadow levels, glass surfaces or gradients. Reuse Soft, Medium and Strong, or go flat.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use the `.btn-*`, `card`, `chip`, `badge` and `input-field` utilities from `index.css` before writing new Tailwind stacks.",
      "**Do** keep every interactive control at 48px or larger.",
      "**Do** set rupee amounts and counts in `font-mono` or `tabular-nums`.",
      "**Do** use Lily Leaf for paid, served and available states, and Roasted Coffee for the next action.",
      "**Do** define dark-mode colours by re-toning tokens under `.dark`, keeping them warm.",
      "**Do** use the shared motion utilities (`animate-*`, `useCountUp`, `useListPresence`) and `--ease-settle` rather than new keyframes or curves.",
      "**Do** give every async surface a plain-language error with a retry (`describeApiError`), and never lose what someone typed."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** set prices, buttons or form labels in Quesha.",
      "**Don't** introduce cool neutral greys (`neutral-800`, `bg-white` without a dark override) in either theme.",
